WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.869
-My next guest is about
to kick off his fifth season

00:00:03.869 --> 00:00:06.206
as Jughead Jones on The CW's
hit show "Riverdale,"

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:09.375
which returns
January 20th at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:11.944
Here's my man, Cole Sprouse!

00:00:11.944 --> 00:00:14.981
Oh! [ Laughs ]

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:17.916
Yeah, you did it.
You did it to me again.

00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:18.918
Oh, my God. I love it.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:20.587
-All the way
back from Peru, man.

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:25.658
-You've outdone yourself, buddy.
I'm so happy to see you.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:28.360
You know, I have an interesting
fact for you, Cole.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.363
Today is January 15th.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:35.001
And did you know that your first
solo appearance on this show,

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:37.737
a few years ago,
was also on January 15th?

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.539
-Really?
-You even drew a picture of me.

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.108
You drew a portrait of me
at the time.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.876
I don't know if you remember.
I saved it.

00:00:43.876 --> 00:00:46.679
-And this is it.
-I hope so. Oh, geez.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:50.616
I must admit, I've gotten
a lot, lot better since then.

00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:52.718
And next time I get to see you

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:55.254
and be blessed
with your presence in person,

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.889
I have another one
coming for you.

00:00:56.889 --> 00:00:59.592
It's my little gift
every time I come on the show.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.829
And by the way,
January 15th is now my day.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.064
-Cole Sprouse Day?
-It's my day. Yes.

00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:07.767
-January 15th is Cole Sprouse
Day on "The Tonight Show."

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.302
Every year, you will be here?

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:12.371
-Regardless of if I'm in Peru
or I'm locked up in prison,

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:15.408
I'll find a way
to make sure that I call you.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.042
-At least we got a phone call.

00:01:17.042 --> 00:01:19.045
That's just --
That's a guarantee, buddy.

00:01:19.045 --> 00:01:20.280
-Yeah.
-Please.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:23.816
-And maybe some bail,
if I'm actually in jail.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:26.352
Help me out.
-Where are you now, though?

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.789
Are you filming "Riverdale" or
you're quarantining?

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:32.992
-I am quarantining,
so I am back up in Vancouver.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:37.730
We start the second half
of the fifth season on Monday.

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:40.132
So I'm almost out of
the lockdown.

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:42.234
-I wanted to ask you
about something I heard

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.070
and I never knew.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.238
It's about you
and your brother.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:49.175
Is it true that you were
named after Nat King Cole

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.278
and your brother
was named after Dylan Thomas?

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.681
-You know, I've heard people --
Now, Dylan Thomas

00:01:54.681 --> 00:01:56.415
is probably way more legitimate,

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:57.917
because his middle name
is Thomas.

00:01:57.917 --> 00:02:01.554
But Nat King Cole --
I've heard Cole Porter.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.623
I think that used
to be something when Dylan and I

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:06.159
were going through our,
like, young-child-star

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:07.560
publicity circuit.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.995
My mom would just say it because
it sounded artsy, you know?

00:02:09.995 --> 00:02:13.065
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.

00:02:13.065 --> 00:02:16.335
-I'm really just named
after, like, cabbage, coleslaw.

00:02:16.335 --> 00:02:18.504
That's the definition
of my name.

00:02:18.504 --> 00:02:20.974
It comes from cabbage farmer,
I think, is --

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:26.545
-But Cole and Dylan --
they're great names.

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:28.547
-I think Cole's pretty great.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:31.583
I think Dylan
could use a little work.

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:34.020
-Dude, you and your brother,
by the way, are --

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.322
Your brother's
coming back to TV.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:39.192
He's in the
new Mindy Kaling show.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.294
And, yeah, it was big news.

00:02:41.294 --> 00:02:42.961
And then I don't know
if you remember

00:02:42.961 --> 00:02:44.997
what you commented on Twitter,
because I follow both.

00:02:44.997 --> 00:02:47.300
Do you remember
what you said?

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:50.836
-Yeah. I asked him
what the crew was going to do

00:02:50.836 --> 00:02:54.907
when they find out
he's just not funny.

00:02:54.907 --> 00:02:56.408
-You go back and forth.

00:02:56.408 --> 00:02:58.544
And I was actually going
to show you some examples,

00:02:58.544 --> 00:03:00.546
because this one thing --

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:02.982
You troll each other and, like,
roast each other online.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.551
This one time, you asked
your brother, @dylansprouse,

00:03:05.551 --> 00:03:08.721
"Were you Zack or Cody?"

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:12.592
Now, that's funny in itself.
I give props for that.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:17.796
I give a like on that one.
I give a couple snaps.

00:03:17.796 --> 00:03:20.099
But then your brother responded,
and he said,

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.434
"I don't remember, actually.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.569
I was too busy
carrying the show on my back."

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:27.706
[ Laughs ]
That got the clap from me there.

00:03:27.706 --> 00:03:29.408
That was fantastic.

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:30.510
Did this start on social media

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.345
or is this always
just a brother thing?

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:35.848
-No. I mean,
this is how I feel like

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:39.018
healthy brother
relationships end up

00:03:39.018 --> 00:03:40.018
speaking to each other.

00:03:40.018 --> 00:03:42.288
-Yeah, a healthy ribbing.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.789
-And we keep each other,
accountable,

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:45.091
keep each other humble.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.494
But, yeah, it hasn't gotten

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.029
pushed too far yet,
though, which is good.

00:03:50.029 --> 00:03:52.331
I'm always, like --
I'm always nervous

00:03:52.331 --> 00:03:53.966
that one day, one of us
is going to say something

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:56.769
that really, like, stings
a little bit too deep.

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:58.771
And we'll get
one of those calls like,

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.907
"Why would you do that,
dude, to the public?"

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:05.578
-"You took it too far, man.
You took it too far.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:08.714
It was funny,
but you took it too far."

00:04:08.714 --> 00:04:10.216
I want to talk about
"Riverdale."

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.517
-Okay.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:14.353
-This season is about
to jump ahead to the future.

00:04:14.353 --> 00:04:16.489
We have a big-time jump.
Yeah.

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:18.757
-I'm excited.
Explain what's happening.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:20.192
-I'm excited for it, too.

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:23.329
So, we had to shut down,

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:28.033
obviously,
because of the COVID lockdown,

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.002
at the final three episodes
of last season.

00:04:30.002 --> 00:04:32.338
So the first three episodes
of this new season

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:34.674
are us finishing those ones.

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:35.808
-Wow.

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.377
-And in Episode 4,
we do a big-time jump

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:42.115
and we all leave Riverdale
at the end of Episode 3

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.916
and come back seven years later.

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.952
So I actually do get to play
roughly my age,

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:48.087
which is wonderful.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:52.125
-Yeah! The first episode
is the prom, and --

00:04:52.125 --> 00:04:55.761
-Yeah. The day
we actually shot the prom

00:04:55.761 --> 00:04:59.265
was the last day before we got
the official shutdown

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:01.099
and were all sent back
to the States.

00:05:01.099 --> 00:05:04.537
-Wow. What a send-off.

00:05:04.537 --> 00:05:05.838
-Yeah, It was kind of funny.

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:09.275
Well, you know, we celebrated
like it was a real prom.

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.343
We were pouring some drinks.
We were having some fun.

00:05:11.343 --> 00:05:14.246
We were singing karaoke.
It was a really wonderful time.

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:17.517
And then we got
the shutdown next day.

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.852
And so, in some strange
kind of way,

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:25.591
we had all celebrated
and reveled without knowing that

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:29.228
that was going to be kind of
this life-changing event.

00:05:29.228 --> 00:05:31.730
And we finished the
prom and then we all kind of

00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:34.300
went on our separate ways for
the entirety of the quarantine.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.936
-So when people watch that,
it has another --

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.804
like, another
special meaning to it.

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:40.639
I want to show
everyone a clip, buddy.

00:05:40.639 --> 00:05:41.840
Here's Cole Sprouse in

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:44.143
the season premiere of
"Riverdale."

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:45.144
Take a look.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.446
-No, I won't help you.
-No, no.

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:49.749
Cheryl, it's not
an actual snuff film.

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:50.850
It's an act.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:52.718
It's a way
to get closer to the auteur,

00:05:52.718 --> 00:05:55.621
the person who's been creating
those re-enactment videos,

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:59.058
including the one with
Jason and your father.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:02.327
-I do want to expose
that defiler.

00:06:02.327 --> 00:06:03.496
What's this movie about anyway?

00:06:03.496 --> 00:06:06.565
-Uh, it's a classic tale,
one as old as time.

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:08.067
A girl meets a boy,

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:09.802
boy promises
to make girl a star,

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:13.005
and -- and the
boy kills the girl.

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.307
-[ Chuckles ]
Charming.

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:17.209
Okay, but I'll need a wig.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:19.512
I don't want anyone to recognize
me by my signature red mane.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.981
-Okay.

00:06:21.981 --> 00:06:24.417
-Cole Sprouse,
Season 5 of "Riverdale"

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:27.220
premieres this Wednesday at
8:00 p.m. on The CW.

